\section{The \calxlogname.tex library}
\RaisedLabel{sec:calxlog}

\localtableofcontents

\subsection{Introduction}

This package provides logarithms, exponentials and fractional powers for
use within \csbxint{floateval} (and \csbxint{eval}).

The first release of \xintexprname supporting logarithms and
exponentials was |1.3e| (|2019/04/05|). It is automatically loaded by
\xintexprname.  Since |2.0a1| |2026/11/01| the maximal supported precision
is of \dtt{100} digits.

The \func{ln} alias, \func{expm1}, \func{log1p}, hyperbolic functions,
and their reciprocals were added at release |1.4p| (March 2026).

At \csbxint{theDigits} set to \dtt{8} (or less), the computations are
targeting a slighlty degraded accuracy (roughly at 8 digits, only about
95\% of values are correctly rounded, compared to 99.5\% for |P>8|.  In
both cases the error is never more tha 1ulp.

