%
% Dispatch as for \CALX_nadd: \CALX_nmul_x writes X followed by 1;!\xint:,
% \CALX_nmul_y grabs P's list and Q's header; jumpers \CALX_nmul_zero,
% \CALX_nmul_sp (P one block: Q stays in place), \CALX_nmul_sq (Q one
% block), \CALX_nmul_xq (iteration over P: Q's list grabbed); inline
% default: iteration over Q, left in place. A one-block factor y uses
% \CALX_verysmallmul if y<22, else \CALX_smallmul (y=1 included).
%
% Choice of the iterated operand: the rule of xintcore's
% \XINT_mul_checklengths, transcribed with X=Q, Y=P by default (A=P, B=Q in
% xintcore): exchange if m<n and (m-1)(n-m)<383, or if m>=n and
% (n-1)(m-n)>383.
