%(
%  \CALX_fmul{P}{X}{Y}   -> <space>Z    Z = round_P(round_P(X) round_P(Y))
%:  \CALX_fmulu{P}{X}{Y}  -> <space>Z    (X, Y finite F, at most P digits)
%:  \CALX_fmulx{X}{Y}     -> <space>Z    exact product (X, Y finite F)
%:  \CALX_faddx{X}{Y}     -> <space>Z    exact sum (X, Y finite F)
%:  \CALX_fsubx{X}{Y}     -> <space>Z    exact difference
%)
% Z: F or I value.
%
% \CALX_fmul{P}{X}{Y} (use with \romannumeral0, X and Y f-expanded):
% round_P(round_P(X) round_P(Y)), round half away from zero, as xint's
% \XINTinFloatMul[P] (xint 1.2k and later).
%
% Special values first (\CALX_fm_sp$empty: I? propagates, inf times zero
% signals InvalidOperation, otherwise I+ or I- by the product of the
% signs), then zero.
%
