% replaced by its top P significant digits A, rounded, as two blocks
% (A = Ah B + Al), and a decimal exponent: X = A 10^(8e + z) (\CALX_fm_xvi
% for P = 16, \CALX_fm_ex otherwise). The product of the two A's is computed
% by \CALX_fm_k (32 digits), then rounded to P digits and put back in the
% native float format by \CALX_fm_r. Otherwise: \CALX_fm_big (P <= 20:
% one product of 20 digit operands, 20 < P <= 34: three such products,
% P > 34: generic).
%
