% \CALX_fm_nsx) and writes it back after Y, padded with two zero blocks
% and closed by \iffalse{\fi} (the closing brace of the \expanded opened
% by \CALX_fm_nc), then {P}. \CALX_fm_ntag reads the tag of Y (special:
% jumper \CALX_fm_nsy). \CALX_fm_nc grabs Y's list and X's header; X's
