% 8, and multiplied by products of 4, 3, 2 or 1 consecutive integers
% (each product < 10^8; \CALX_ffac_smallmul, own small multiplication
% which reports a carry). When a carry creates a block Q + 1 the least
% significant one is dropped and E increases by 8. \CALX_ffac_increaseP
% (\CALX_fpfac_increaseP) chooses Q from the target p and a factor c
% (their last two arguments) so that the relative error is below
% c 10^(-p-1): 8Q >= p + 9 + k, k the number of digits of the count of
% products divided by c (\CALX_ndig). The blocks are those of a native
